# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SECOND PASS · 10 September 2026
#
# The first audit went after files nothing links to. This one goes after whole
# folders that ship because nobody ever said not to: the generators, their
# source data, and the two rendering tools. None of it is served, and none of
# it is read by a function at runtime -- which was checked rather than assumed.
# The complete set of paths any serverless function opens is:
#
#     assets/dict-index.json      assets/menu-index.json
#     i18n/en.json                lights/all.json
#     node/*                      study/*
#     reels/index.json            nodes-index.js
#     noor-guide-data.js          tools/reels/quran-uthmani.json
#                                 tools/reels/verses.txt
#
# Those last two are why tools/ is trimmed rather than dropped: vercel.json
# lists them in includeFiles, and a parent directory that never arrives cannot
# have a file included out of it. Everything else under tools/ goes.
#
# api/_nightshift.js names "build/lights-*.json" in a string. It is telling a
# reader where a light was written, not opening it; grep for readJSON, readText
# and readFileSync across api/ and build/ appears in none of them.
#
# About 11.5 MB of a 54 MB deployment.
/scripts/
/build/
/.build-src/
/.github/
/tools/films/
/tools/reels/web/
/tools/reels/__pycache__/
/tools/reels/plan.json
/tools/reels/know.json
/tools/reels/light.json
/tools/reels/calendar.json

# Superseded, and still being uploaded. The menu moved into the shell that
# noor-fx.js draws on every page, and its search opens assets/noor-search.js;
# no page has linked either of these since. scripts/nav49.py was still writing
# the tags for them into a header no page carries any more -- that is fixed in
# the same commit, because a file that stops shipping and a script that keeps
# asking for it is a 404 waiting for whoever runs the generator next.
/assets/noor-menu.js
/assets/noor-menu.css

# The card faces. They are read by scripts/gen-card-fonts.py, which embeds
# them into api/_cardfont.js as bytes; the browser never asks for the files.
/assets/fonts/

# The lantern, twice. assets/noor-lantern.js is on nine pages and stays; this
# is the older copy at the root, which nothing has linked since it moved.
/lantern.js
